                                                                                                                                                                                            <div class="ielts-reading-question-item">
                                                                                                    
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                </div>
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            <div class="ielts-standalone-q ielts-multi-q" data-multi-qnums="19,20"><div class="ielts-q-header"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">19</strong> <strong class="ielts-q-badge">20</strong><span class="ielts-q-title"><span>Which  of the following statements are made in the text about the Amsterdam bike-sharing scheme of 1999?</span></div><div class="ielts-checkbox-group"><label class="ielts-checkbox-btn"><input type="checkbox" data-multi-qnums="19,20" data-limit="2" value="A"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>A</strong> It was initially opposed by a government department.</span></label><label class="ielts-checkbox-btn"><input type="checkbox" data-multi-qnums="19,20" data-limit="2" value="B"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>B</strong> It failed when a partner in the scheme withdrew support.</span></label><label class="ielts-checkbox-btn"><input type="checkbox" data-multi-qnums="19,20" data-limit="2" value="C"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>C</strong> It aimed to be more successful than the Copenhagen scheme.</span></label><label class="ielts-checkbox-btn"><input type="checkbox" data-multi-qnums="19,20" data-limit="2" value="D"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>D</strong> It was made possible by a change in people’s attitudes.</span></label><label class="ielts-checkbox-btn"><input type="checkbox" data-multi-qnums="19,20" data-limit="2" value="E"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>E</strong> It attracted interest from a range of bike designers.</span></label></div></div></div>
