                                                                                                                                                            <h2 class="ielts-reading-question-section-heading">
                                            Questions 9-13                                                                                                                                                
                                                                                                                                    </h2>
                                        <div class="ielts-reading-question-section-content">
                                            <div class="ielts-reading-section-content-wrapper"><p>Complete the notes below</p>
<p>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</p>
<p><em>Write your answers in boxes on your answer sheet.</em></p>
<p class="ielts-reading-passage-subhead"><strong><strong>Alexander Henderson</strong></strong></p>
<p><strong>Early life</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>was born in Scotland in 1831 – father was a <span class="ielts-reading-question-item"><span class="ielts-inline-input-wrap"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">9</strong><input type="text" data-qnum="9" name="question_9" class="ielts-inline-input" placeholder="[9] javob..." autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"></span></span></li>
<li>trained as an accountant, emigrated to Canada in 1855</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Start of a photographic career</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>opened up a photographic studio in 1866</li>
<li>took photos of city life, but preferred landscape photography</li>
<li>people bought Henderson’s photos because photography took up considerable time and the <span class="ielts-reading-question-item"><span class="ielts-inline-input-wrap"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">10</strong><input type="text" data-qnum="10" name="question_10" class="ielts-inline-input" placeholder="[10] javob..." autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"></span></span> was heavy</li>
<li>the photographs Henderson sold were <span class="ielts-reading-question-item"><span class="ielts-inline-input-wrap"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">11</strong><input type="text" data-qnum="11" name="question_11" class="ielts-inline-input" placeholder="[11] javob..." autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"></span></span> or souvenirs</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Travelling as a professional photographer</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>travelled widely in Quebec and Ontario in 1870s and 1880s</li>
<li>took many trips along eastern rivers in a <span class="ielts-reading-question-item"><span class="ielts-inline-input-wrap"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">12</strong><input type="text" data-qnum="12" name="question_12" class="ielts-inline-input" placeholder="[12] javob..." autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"></span></span></li>
<li>worked for Canadian railways between 1875 and 1897</li>
<li>worked for CPR in 1885 and photographed the <span class="ielts-reading-question-item"><span class="ielts-inline-input-wrap"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">13</strong><input type="text" data-qnum="13" name="question_13" class="ielts-inline-input" placeholder="[13] javob..." autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"></span></span> and the railway at Rogers Pass</li>
</ul>
</div>                                        </div>
                                        <div class="ielts-reading-questions">
                                                                                                                                                                                            <div class="ielts-reading-question-item">
                                                                                                    
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                </div>
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            <div class="ielts-reading-question-item">
                                                                                                    
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                </div>
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            <div class="ielts-reading-question-item">
                                                                                                    
